---
import { profile } from '../data/portfolio';
import SectionRail from './SectionRail.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="about">
  <SectionRail label="About" />
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h2>Full-stack engineer who owns products <span class="accent">end to end</span>.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-bio reveal" data-delay="1">
        <p>
          I'm a <b>full-stack engineer</b> working mainly in TypeScript: <b>React and Next.js</b>
          interfaces, <b>Node.js APIs</b> with <b>PostgreSQL and SQLite</b> behind them, and Docker,
          Nginx and GitHub Actions to ship. At <b>LYIK Technologies</b> — where I was recently
          promoted to Senior Engineer — I work across three products: the v2 form-filling platform,
          the v3 configurable platform and its admin dashboard, and a compliance dashboard I owned
          across the whole stack, from UI and API to database and deployment.
        </p>
        <p>
          That ownership is the part I care about most: <b>gathering requirements directly from
          customers</b>, leading the discussions that align backend, QA and product, taking a product
          from that first conversation through architecture, build and <b>production deployment</b>,
          and <b>mentoring</b> the intern who built features on top of it. The engineering underneath —
          a config-driven dashboard renderer, a permission <b>guardrail</b> system, the
          <b>maker-checker</b> workflow, the form <b>engines</b> (rules, derive, actions, navigator) and
          their test suites — exists to make complex requirements feel effortless to use.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside work I go wider on purpose: a central <b>authentication service</b> (OIDC, MFA and
          an audit trail on ZITADEL and PostgreSQL), <b>local-first desktop apps</b> in Tauri and
          Rust, <b>Android apps</b> in Expo, and command-line tools. Whichever layer the problem
          lives in, I can pick it up and ship it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-side">
        <div class="stat-card reveal" data-delay="2">
          <div class="stat-num">30%+</div>
          <div class="stat-label">efficiency gains delivered through client-facing platform development</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card fact-card reveal" data-delay="3">
          <div class="fc-label"><svg class="ic" data-lucide="graduation-cap"></svg> Education</div>
          <div class="fc-value">{profile.education} — {profile.educationSchool}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card fact-card reveal" data-delay="3">
          <div class="fc-label"><svg class="ic" data-lucide="languages"></svg> Languages</div>
          <div class="chip-row">
            {profile.languages.map((l) => <span class="chip">{l}</span>)}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
